(g) cooperate with the Authority and any other contractors or third parties engaged in work on or near the Network.

4.2 The Contractor shall comply with the Rail Infrastructure Management Act 2023 (Vic) and any regulations or guidelines made under that Act, including any requirements relating to the approval of maintenance contractors.

4.3 The Contractor shall obtain and maintain all licences, permits, and approvals required for the performance of the Services, at its own cost.

5. AUTHORITY’S OBLIGATIONS

5.1 The Authority shall:

(a) provide the Contractor with access to the Network and any relevant documentation, including plans, drawings, and asset registers, as reasonably required for the performance of the Services;

(b) ensure that any Track Possessions requested by the Contractor in accordance with clause 10 are scheduled and coordinated with other users of the Network;

(c) notify the Contractor of any known hazards or conditions on the Network that may affect the performance of the Services;

(d) pay the Contract Price in accordance with Schedule 2; and

